# Exemplar 31 — root an analysis in place, chell style.
#
# Registered plugins are executables: /bin lists them, and running one
# inside a data directory creates the feed (with a pl-dircopy root),
# attaches the plugin, and schedules it — no ids change hands, which is
# what makes this expressible as a static script at all. Point it at a
# directory of DICOMs (for example a pulled series) for a real
# conversion; the flow is identical for any plugin and any data.
#
# Manual exemplar: it creates a feed the CUBE keeps, so run it, inspect
# the result, and clean up when done. The residue-free, self-cleaning
# form of this workflow (with polling and verification) is the TS
# exemplar 03_feedDcm2niix.
#
# Connect once first, then:
#   chell -e -f exemplars/chell/31_feed_inplace.chell

# Which dcm2niix builds does this CUBE offer? Every registered plugin
# also appears as an executable under /bin.
plugin search dcm2niix

# Enter the directory whose contents should root the feed.
cd ~/data/SAG-anon

# Run the plugin as a command. chell creates the feed from the current
# directory and chains the analysis onto its root; the context after
# `--` sets feed-level fields.
pl-dcm2niix-v1.0.2 -- feed_title="SAG anon conversion"

# The feed exists immediately; the job appears under /proc as it runs.
feed list --limit 1
ls /proc/jobs
